    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d937">

                <pb facs="1088" n="1008" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1008"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Eddy.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee states that the secretary of the mission board telegraphs that the
                    money needed for Miss Stone’s ransom will undoubtedly be <pb facs="1089"
                        n="1009" xml:id="pg1009"/> raised by popular subscription, which is already
                    begun; that Mr. Eddy’s efforts are warmly approved; that Russian cooperation,
                    especially at Sofia, is most valuable and is cordially welcomed, as is also the
                    weighty aid of the other ambassadors.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
